      "content": "it's just interesting that when you say \"lack of awareness\" or \"professional intelligence,\" it feels like you're saying that if someone doesn't use Standard American English, they're inherently less competent or less educated. \n\nif Candidate B was a white guy from a rural area using different slang, would you still judge their \"professional intelligence\" so harshly? or is it more that this specific way of speaking—which is common in many Black communities—is being automatically flagged as \"unpolished\" or \"unprofessional\" by your standards? basically, are you saying that the dialect itself is a marker of lower intelligence?",
